  "rules": [
    "Model exhibits a persistent upward bias when recent history shows high volatility (range > 10 EUR) and mixed sentiment signals; true outcomes often deviate -5 to -8 EUR from forecasts.",
    "When sentiment shifts from positive (1.0) to negative (-1.0) within the last 3 days, the model fails to capture immediate mean reversion, resulting in significant overshoots of +4 to +6 EUR.",
    "The model displays a lag in reacting to sudden price spikes; true outcomes frequently reverse direction within 5-7 days after a forecast peak, whereas the model continues trending upward.",
    "In high-volatility regimes (history std dev > 3), the model's linear extrapolation is invalid; apply a correction factor of -0.15 EUR per day for the first 10 days post-forecast.",
    "Sentiment spikes (1.0) followed by neutralization (0.0) within 48 hours indicate a false breakout signal; reduce forecast trajectory by 20% in these scenarios."
  ]
}
